# the compilation of a module for a target, the entry mach calls
#
# the pipeline is the one the target's family states, chosen by the target's
# declarations, never its name. what depends on the target alone is made once
# per build, in a `Prepared` the caller holds across every module it
# compiles: `open` reads the family registry and takes the one family that
# admits the target, refusing a target none or several admit before anything
# runs, lists the owners of the registry's opcode rows and has the family
# open the build, whose back end validates its static tables there. each
# `compile` of a checked build refuses a module holding an opcode row a
# family that does not serve the target owns, before the schedule and before
# the back end, a rule the caller upholds otherwise. it runs the neutral
# prefix and the family's rows over the build, and hands the scheduled module
# to the family's back end, so the schedule and the back end read the one
# build. before the back end, a module holding a function
# that requires constant time is refused when the target's set classifies no
# timing, as spir-v's, and when the ir's oblivious check finds a secret where
# it may hold none, so every family keeps the discipline, wasm's whose timing
# is not guaranteed among them. `write` lays the object out in the default
# object format the target's system states, through the build's registry of
# mink's formats.

